Justin hey Walt here with a GameSpot  breaking news update the witcher 3 wild  hunt has been officially delayed until  February 2015 CD projekt red's hotly  anticipated role-playing game the  witcher 3 wild hunt has been delayed  from fall later this year to February  2015 CD Projekt RED management announced  the news today in an open letter to fans  the letter reads ever since we started  working on the third installment in the  witcher franchise it's been our aim to  produce a title that would take our 11  years of experience in creating RPGs and  distill them into a quintessence into a  game that would effectively crown those  years we've created a story that flows  naturally cinematically rendered it an  amazing sound and visuals while  preserving full freedom of choice we  recently reexamined what we had achieved  thus far and faced a choice about the  game's final release date the decision  we made was difficult thoroughly  considered and ultimately clear and  obvious we concluded that a few  additional months will let us achieve  the quality that will satisfy us the  quality gamers expect from us  consequently we've set the release date  of the witcher 3 wild hunt for February  2015 you can read the entire letter on  gamespot and we'll keep you updated as  this story develops
 

